From 1b1c4065649f43b2b3fc90e0a5e2f1d468491de7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 05:17:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 220/254] perf(cpu): execute AVX2 layout ops natively
 (avx2-layout-native)

Add a PXLD-v2 descriptor-driven native plane for reshape/view/contiguous/
transpose/slice plus split/concat on the AVX2 backend for f32/bf16/int8,
mirroring the verified SVE256/AVX-512 semantics.  The native contract
predicate is shared by artifact metadata and the runtime dispatch, so a
declared kernel is the executed kernel; unsupported dtypes stay on the
vector-common host reference with an explicit metadata reason.  f32/bf16
lanes reproduce the host reference's Python-float round trip (including
signaling-NaN quieting) so native outputs are byte-identical to the
host_reference baseline; contiguous copies and split/concat segments use
AVX2 integer-lane quieting.  The pre-existing packed rank-2 transpose plane
is kept byte-for-byte (it preserves sNaN payloads; recorded as a boundary).
Zero-copy view aliasing is stat-only and remains disabled.  Bump artifact
payload 4->5 and the native ABI marker to :6.
