+ * Native layout / split / concat plane (artifact payload version 5).
+ *
+ * The descriptor wire is the same little-endian ``PXLD`` v2 payload the
+ * verified SVE256/AVX-512 runners consume: a 40-byte header followed by the
+ * rank-sized input_shape / output_shape / source_strides / permutation /
+ * slice_starts / slice_steps arrays.  The Python runtime serializes one
+ * descriptor per plan digest and never materializes a per-element index map;
+ * the kernel decodes and re-validates the descriptor before it touches
+ * memory and returns a non-zero status for any violation.
+ *
+ * f32/bf16 lanes reproduce the vector-common host reference exactly: the
+ * reference round-trips every element through a Python float, which is the
+ * identity for finite/subnormal/quiet-NaN values and quiets a signaling NaN.
+ * The contiguous copy kind (reshape/view/contiguous) and the split/concat
+ * segment copies use an AVX2 lane path with pure integer bit operations, so
+ * the quieting stays bit-exact and no FP exception is raised; int8 has no
+ * value conversion, so its lanes are raw byte copies.
+ * ---------------------------------------------------------------------- */
+#define PTX_AVX2_LAYOUT_DESC_VERSION 2U
+#define PTX_AVX2_LAYOUT_DESC_HEADER_BYTES 40U
+#define PTX_AVX2_LAYOUT_MAX_RANK 64U
+#define PTX_AVX2_LAYOUT_KIND_COPY 0U
+#define PTX_AVX2_LAYOUT_KIND_TRANSPOSE 1U
+#define PTX_AVX2_LAYOUT_KIND_SLICE 2U
